So if I have two equations:
1) C + R = 36
2) 2C + 4R = 100

I can solve these using substitution or elimination. Maybe substitution is easier here. From equation 1, I can express C as 36 - R and substitute into equation 2. Let me try that.

Substituting C = 36 - R into the second equation gives:
2*(36 - R) + 4R = 100
72 - 2R + 4R = 100
