Wait, but are these methods consistent? The first method uses place value, the second uses positional system concepts, and the third uses algebra. All three lead to the conclusion that multiplying by 10 adds a zero at the end because of the base-10 structure. Yeah, they all align. So the answer is that multiplying by 10 increases the place value of each digit by one, which is achieved by appending a zero. Different perspectives confirm the same result.
