Third method. Maybe using tables or listing possible numbers. For example, start by assuming all 29 are chickens. Then legs would be 58. We need 84 legs, so we need 26 more legs. Since replacing a chicken with a dog adds 2 legs, we need 26/2=13 dogs. So again, 13 dogs and 16 chickens. Same answer.

